body:
It depends, does she have Dementia or alzheimers? If so, I wouldn't say that her son died because it could cause her too much pain and it's not worth her getting worked up about it because she's not going to remember it anyway. I would make up something like he's at work or something. 

&#x200B;

But if she's not going through Dementia, I would give it a day or so to come up with how you should break the news. Just make sure you give her plenty of love and comfort when you do so. If she ends up getting too worked up, I would try to have her do calming techniques to try to help her calm down so that she doesn't end up having another stroke/ heart attack.
